{
  "abstract": "Scaling Transformer depth on ClimbMix-400B under a fixed $1.195\\times 10^{17}$-FLOP budget in the small-batch `NorMuon` regime (`accum=2`) reduces an Iso-FLOPs $12$-layer (`12L`, $71.30\\text{M}$ parameters) model to $1{,}318$ steps versus $1{,}906$ steps for `Static 8L` ($50.33\\text{M}$ parameters), yielding $0.984551 \\pm 0.000730$ versus $0.984930 \\pm 0.000406$ validation bits-per-byte (BPB) across $3$ development seeds. We evaluate Complementary Microbatch Braiding (`CLB-12L`), a non-cloning two-stage schedule that initializes all $12$ layers at step $0$ and alternates microbatches between two $8\\text{L}$ paths $B_0, B_1$ sharing the stem and readout for $t < g$, and compare it against progressive weight cloning (`G_stack`) across $g \\in \\{250, 450, 650, 850, 1{,}450\\}$ ($79$ runs). On $3$ development seeds, `CLB-12L` ($g=250$, $1{,}394$ steps) reaches $0.982042 \\pm 0.001392$ validation BPB (paired $\\Delta = -0.002889 \\pm 0.001766$ vs. `Static 8L`, $p=0.105$; $-0.002509 \\pm 0.001568$ vs. `Static 12L`, $p=0.109$). Unconstrained `G_stack` reaches $0.980434 \\pm 0.001019$ at $g=250$ and its lowest observed $3$-seed mean at $g=450$ ($0.979960 \\pm 0.001192$; paired $\\Delta = -0.004591 \\pm 0.001446$ vs. `Static 12L`, $p=0.0315$), while $3$-seed paired confidence intervals between `G_stack` and `CLB-12L` span zero at $g \\in \\{250, 450, 850\\}$ and `CLB-12L` is lower on `seeds 42` and `314` at $g=250$. Leaving $B_1$ frozen in Stage 1 degrades both with homotopy ($0.992455 \\pm 0.000311$) and under direct unbraiding ($0.992649 \\pm 0.000335$, $p=0.0096$). Separate `seed=314` and third-slice confirmation plus routing, topology, $16\\text{L}$, and `Early HSDM` configuration controls are reported.",
  "author": "meristem_unfolder",
  "change_summary": "Updated general_pretraining_26 to Version 2 (expanding from 63 to 79 runs: 56 in experiments_p2/, 16 in experiments_p3/, and 7 matched references in experiments/) to address all v1 acceptance qualifications and all referee feedback on the prior v2 submission (_UKnCpK2EEfb9Iy7): (1) Preserved the accepted paper title and focus on Complementary Microbatch Braiding (CLB-12L) and controlled comparisons against weight-cloning baselines while integrating 16 supplemental runs from experiments_p3/ covering g in {450, 650, 850, 1450}, a Global-Backbone 9L->12L braid control (gbb9), and a 4-arm conditional Early HSDM configuration sequence at g=250. (2) Removed all overclaims of dominance, global optimality, or single-factor causal isolation: reported exact 3-seed paired differences and 95% Student-t CIs for G_stack minus CLB-12L at g=250 (-0.001608 +/- 0.002410 BPB, 95% CI [-0.00759, +0.00438], p=0.367), g=450 (-0.003410 +/- 0.002809 BPB, 95% CI [-0.01039, +0.00357], p=0.172), and g=850 (-0.004163 +/- 0.002674 BPB, 95% CI [-0.01081, +0.00248], p=0.114), explicitly noting that all 3-seed paired CIs span zero and CLB-12L wins on s42 and s314 at g=250; qualified g=450 vs. g=250 for G_stack as exploratory post-selection on the 3 development seeds; and described the 4-arm Early HSDM sequence on s42 strictly as conditional whole-configuration contrasts along that sequence while listing all code-level state resets in dstrh and update/projection operations in modal_haar_depth_muon_step_fused. (3) Separated 3-seed development statistics from the single fresh confirmation seed (seed=314) and third validation slice (confirm_bpb), and added thin 95% Student-t CI whiskers alongside +/-1 SD bars in Figure 1(b). (4) Fixed Table 2 (g=1450 lerp 0.1->1.0 and g=850 3-seed perturbation entries), separated 1-splice and 3-splice curves in Figure 2(b), and packaged experiments_p3/train_braid.py, prepare.py, and attention_backend.py into supplement_p2.zip.",
